  urldate = {2026-06-29},
  abstract = {Let \$(X,{$\omega$})\$ be a closed symplectic manifold. A loop \${$\varphi$}: S\textasciicircum 1 \textbackslash to \textbackslash mathrm\textbraceleft Diff\textbraceright (X)\$ of diffeomorphisms of \$X\$ defines a fibration \${$\pi$}: P\_{$\varphi$} \textbackslash to S\textasciicircum 2\$. By applying Gromov-Witten theory to moduli spaces of holomorphic sections of \${$\pi\$$}, Lalonde, McDuff and Polterovich proved that if \${$\varphi\$$} lifts to the Hamiltonian group \$\textbackslash mathrm\textbraceleft Ham\textbraceright (X,{$\omega$})\$, then the rational cohomology of \$P\_{$\varphi\$$} splits additively. We prove, with the same assumptions, that the \$\textbackslash mathbb\textbraceleft E\textbraceright\$-generalised cohomology of \$P\_{$\varphi\$$} splits additively for any complex-oriented cohomology theory \$\textbackslash mathbb\textbraceleft E\textbraceright\$, in particular the integral cohomology splits. This class of examples includes all complex projective varieties equipped with a smooth morphism to \$\textbackslash mathbb\textbraceleft CP\textbraceright\textasciicircum 1\$, in which case the analogous rational result was proved by Deligne using Hodge theory. The argument employs virtual fundamental cycles of moduli spaces of sections of \${$\pi\$$} in Morava \$K\$-theory and results from chromatic homotopy theory. Our proof involves a construction of independent interest: we build global Kuranishi charts for moduli spaces of pseudo-holomorphic spheres in \$X\$ in a class \${$\beta\backslash$}in H\_2(X;\textbackslash mathbb\textbraceleft Z\textbraceright )\$, depending on a choice of integral symplectic form \$\textohm\$ on \$X\$ and ample Hermitian line bundle over the moduli space of one-pointed degree \$d = \textbackslash langle \textohm,{$\beta\backslash$}rangle\$ stable genus zero curves in \$\textbackslash mathbb\textbraceleft CP\textbraceright\textasciicircum d\$.},
