  abstract = {The Fano models of Enriques surfaces produce a family of tens of mutually intersecting planes in \$\textbackslash mathbf P\textasciicircum 5\$ with a \$10\$-dimensional moduli space. The latter is linked to several 10-dimensional moduli spaces parametrizing other types of objects: a) cubic fourfolds containing the tens of planes, b) Beauville--Donagi holomorphically symplectic fourfolds, and c) double EPW sextics. The varieties in b) parametrize lines on cubic fourfolds from a). The double EPW sextics are associated, via O'Grady's construction, to Lagrangian subspaces of the Pl\textbackslash "ucker space of the Grassmannian \$Gr(2,\textbackslash mathbf P\textasciicircum 5)\$ spanned by 10 mutually intersecting planes in \$\textbackslash mathbf P\textasciicircum 5\$. These links imply the irreducibility of the moduli space of supermarked Enriques surfaces, where a supermarking is a choice of a minimal generating system of the Picard group of the surface. Also some results are obtained on the variety of tens of mutually intersecting planes, not necessarily associated to Fano models of Enriques surfaces.},
  keywords = {enriques-surfaces,k3-surfaces,lattices,moduli,symplectic-geometry},
